      "note": "Provisional machine alignment by Codex, independent Tibetan-first proposal. The Upali work is treated as a proper title; its name member is literal. rtog pa/dbang and the establishment verbs are matched independently to this row's English, not inferred from comparative dictionary glosses. kha bye is narrowed to open, leaving the supplied possessive in their petals unwrapped. yid 'ong ba is provisionally matched to breathtaking beauty; mchog is omitted because its contribution may be distributed in that poetic wording. The maker-negative is recast as a search: 'ga' med is omitted rather than equated to find or asserted absent. The last two Tibetan conceptual-establishment formulations are compressed into one English creation-of-conceptions formulation; the earlier rtog pas/btags pa/tsam anchors it and the final rtog pa'i dbang gis bzhag par is omitted as distributed repetition. Repeated conception and object spans use explicit English order. Genitive and other omitted grammar is not given invented English. Null rnams marks only plural force fused into objects. C16:806 has matching Tibetan fields but different English vocabulary; no ingestion lineage or independent publication is inferred."
